n\n.cta-section{background:var(--blue);border-radius:16px;padding:56px 48px;text-align:center;margin-bottom:48px;position:relative;overflow:hidden;}\n.cta-section::before{content:'';position:absolute;top:-100px;right:-100px;width:400px;height:400px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);border-radius:50%;}\n.cta-h2{font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(26px,3.5vw,40px);font-weight:900;color:#fff;margin-bottom:14px;letter-spacing:-.025em;position:relative;}\n.cta-h2 em{font-style:italic;font-weight:300;color:#bfdbfe;}\n.cta-body{font-size:16px;color:#bfdbfe;max-width:480px;margin:0 auto 32px;line-height:1.75;position:relative;}\n.cta-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;justify-content:center;position:relative;}\n.btn-cta{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;background:#fff;color:var(--blue);font-size:15px;font-weight:700;padding:15px 30px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;transition:transform .1s;white-space:nowrap;}\n.btn-cta:hover{transform:translateY(-1px);}\n.btn-cta-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;background:transparent;color:#fff;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;padding:15px 24px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3);transition:border-color .15s;white-space:nowrap;}\n.btn-cta-outline:hover{border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.65);}\n.cta-note{font-size:12px;color:#93c5fd;margin-top:16px;position:relative;}\n\n@media(max-width:640px){\n  .hero-inner,.main{padding-left:24px;padding-right:24px;}\n  .trust{padding-left:24px;padding-right:24px;}\n  .trap-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;}\n  .bi-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.bi-card.bonus{grid-column:1;}\n  .also-list,.who-list{grid-template-columns:1fr;}\n  .author{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:32px 24px;}\n  .cta-section{padding:40px 24px;}\n}\n</style>\n\n<div class=\"announce\">Free Big Idea 1 Superpack — no purchase needed. <a href=\"/products/ap-csp-big-idea-1-superpack-free\">Download free →</a>\n</div>\n\n<section class=\"hero\">\n  <div class=\"hero-inner\">\n    <div class=\"hero-kicker\">AP Computer Science Principles · Teacher Superpack</div>\n    <h1>Built from 2,000 hours of<br><em>watching students miss questions.</em>\n</h1>\n    <p class=\"hero-sub\">After tutoring AP CS students for hundreds of hours, I know exactly where they get tripped up on exam day — and exactly what wasn't in their course materials. <strong>I built APCSExamPrep.com to fix that.</strong> The Teacher Superpack brings that same approach into your classroom.</p>\n    <div class=\"hero-actions\">\n      <a href=\"/products/ap-csp-teacher-superpack\" class=\"btn-primary\">Get the Superpack — $249 →</a>\n      <a href=\"/products/ap-csp-big-idea-1-superpack-free\" class=\"btn-ghost\">Free BI1 Preview — no purchase needed</a>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"hero-footnote\">One-time · Instant delivery · Updates through summer 2026 included</div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<div class=\"trust\">\n  <div class=\"trust-inner\">\n    <span class=\"trust-item\">✅ <strong>11+ years</strong> AP CS classroom experience</span>\n    <span class=\"trust-item\">⭐ <strong>5.0</strong> on Wyzant · 499 verified reviews</span>\n    <span class=\"trust-item\">📚 <strong>2,067</strong> tutoring hours</span>\n    <span class=\"trust-item\">📋 <strong>CED-built</strong> from the 2025-2026 AP CSP exam</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<main class=\"main\">\n\n  <section class=\"insight\">\n    <div class=\"kicker\">What 2,000 tutoring hours taught me</div>\n    <h2 class=\"h2\">I've seen every resource. I know where each one leaves students unprepared.</h2>\n    <p class=\"sub\">Tutoring gives you a diagnostic view that classroom teaching alone doesn't. When a student comes to you two weeks before the AP exam, you see exactly which concepts didn't land — and exactly how the resource they used framed those concepts differently from how the exam actually tests them.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"insight-story\">\n      <p class=\"insight-quote\">\"The practice questions I'd been doing all year felt easy. Then I sat down for the actual exam and the questions were phrased completely differently. I didn't recognize them as the same topics.\"</p>\n      <div class=\"insight-attr\">— Pattern I heard from <strong>students across dozens of tutoring sessions</strong>\n</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"trap-grid\">\n      <div class=\"trap-card featured\">\n        <div class=\"trap-num\">The core problem</div>\n        <div class=\"trap-title\">Practice questions that look like AP questions but aren't</div>\n        <div class=\"trap-desc\">College Board has specific phrasing patterns — the I/II/III formats, the predict-first structure, the exact way distractors are built to target real misconceptions. Resources that approximate this pattern leave students surprised by the actual exam.</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"trap-card\">\n        <div class=\"trap-num\">What I see in tutoring</div>\n        <div class=\"trap-title\">Students who worked hard but hit the wrong targets</div>\n        <div class=\"trap-desc\">They completed every assignment. They understood the concepts. But the questions they practiced didn't match how the AP exam asks about those concepts. Effort without exam-accurate targets doesn't produce the scores the effort deserves.</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"trap-card\">\n        <div class=\"trap-num\">The Big Idea 3 pattern</div>\n        <div class=\"trap-title\">Code tracing done right vs done generically</div>\n        <div class=\"trap-desc\">BI3 algorithm questions aren't just \"read the code.\" College Board uses specific structures — nested conditions, loop edge cases, off-by-one patterns — that only appear exam-accurate if built directly from real AP exam question analysis.</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"trap-card\">\n        <div class=\"trap-num\">The BI5 pattern</div>\n        <div class=\"trap-title\">Impact questions students can't answer with facts alone</div>\n        <div class=\"trap-desc\">Students who memorize BI5 vocabulary still miss questions because the exam asks them to apply nuanced reasoning — same effect viewed differently, intended vs unintended, data aggregation scenarios. That reasoning has to be practiced, not just read.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"insight-cta\">\n      <div class=\"insight-cta-title\">What this means for the Superpack</div>\n      <p class=\"insight-cta-body\">Every lesson, every slide, every practice question in the Superpack is built with those tutoring patterns in mind. <strong>The gaps students show up to tutoring with are the gaps this course was designed to close before exam day.</strong> The free Big Idea 1 preview lets you see that approach in practice before spending anything.</p>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"inside\">\n    <div class=\"kicker\">What's included</div>\n    <h2 class=\"h2\">All 5 Big Ideas. One complete course.</h2>\n    <p class=\"sub\">Each Big Idea includes slides and lesson resources aligned to every lesson on APCSExamPrep.com — so your classroom instruction and your students' daily practice reinforce each other.</p>\n    <div class=\"bi-grid\">\n      <div class=\"bi-card free\">\n        <div class=\"free-tag\">Free Preview</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-num\">Big Idea 1</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-title\">Creative Development</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-items\">Slides · Program design · Collaboration · Debugging · Try it before buying anything</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"bi-card\">\n        <div class=\"bi-num\">Big Idea 2</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-title\">Data</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-items\">Slides · Binary · Compression · Data analysis · Visualization</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"bi-card\">\n        <div class=\"bi-num\">Big Idea 3</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-title\">Algorithms &amp; Programming</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-items\">Slides · All 18 topics · Python + AP Pseudocode · Interactive support</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"bi-card\">\n        <div class=\"bi-num\">Big Idea 4</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-title\">Computer Systems &amp; Networks</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-items\">Slides · Internet · Fault tolerance · Parallel computing</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"bi-card\">\n        <div class=\"bi-num\">Big Idea 5</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-title\">Impact of Computing</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-items\">Slides · All 6 topics · Bias · Privacy · Legal · Safe computing</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"bi-card bonus\">\n        <div class=\"bi-num\">Also included</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-title\">APCSExamPrep.com — student access for your class</div>\n        <div class=\"bi-items\">Interactive lessons · 5 exam-aligned MCQs per topic built from tutoring insight · Daily QOTD · Create Task scaffolding · The same practice that closes the gaps tutoring reveals</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"also\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\">\n      <div class=\"also-title\">Every purchase also includes</div>\n      <ul class=\"also-list\">\n        <li>Updates through summer 2026 as content is finalized</li>\n        <li>Create Task scaffolding and rubric guides</li>\n        <li>MCQs built to match AP exam phrasing, not approximate it</li>\n        <li>Direct access to reach me with questions</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <div class=\"honest\">\n    <strong>What you're actually buying:</strong> Slides and lesson resources for all 5 Big Ideas, aligned to every lesson on APCSExamPrep.com. Materials are being finalized through summer 2026 — updates are automatic. Big Idea 1 is a free download. Use it in your classroom first. Buy the rest only if it works for you.\n  </div>\n\n  <section class=\"who\">\n    <div class=\"kicker\">Who this is for</div>\n    <h2 class=\"h2\">Built for AP CSP teachers.</h2>\n    <ul class=\"who-list\">\n      <li>Teachers whose students use APCSExamPrep.com for practice and want classroom instruction built to the same exam-accurate standard</li>\n      <li>First-year AP CSP teachers who want a foundation built from real tutoring insight — not generic content that approximates the exam</li>\n      <li>Experienced teachers who've watched prepared students still get surprised by AP exam phrasing and want to close that gap upstream</li>\n      <li>Department chairs who want consistent, exam-precise materials from a teacher with 2,067 hours of diagnostic AP CS tutoring experience</li>\n    </ul>\n  </section>\n\n  <div class=\"author\">\n    <div class=\"author-av\">TC</div>\n    <div>\n      <div class=\"author-name\">Tanner Crow</div>\n      <div class=\"author-role\">AP CS Teacher &amp; Tutor · 11+ years · Kansas City area</div>\n      <p class=\"author-body\">I've taught AP Computer Science for over a decade and logged 2,067 hours tutoring AP CS students one-on-one, with a 5.0 rating and 499 verified reviews on Wyzant. That tutoring experience gave me a diagnostic view I couldn't get from teaching alone — I saw exactly which concepts students understood but couldn't answer correctly because of how the exam phrases its questions. I built APCSExamPrep.com to close those gaps. The Superpack is that same work packaged as a complete course for your classroom.</p>\n      <div class=\"author-tags\">\n        <span class=\"author-tag\">11+ years AP CS</span>\n        <span class=\"author-tag\">5.0 ★ Wyzant</span>\n        <span class=\"author-tag\">499+ reviews</span>\n        <span class=\"author-tag\">2,067 tutoring hours</span>\n        <span class=\"author-tag\">CED-built from scratch</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"cta-section\">\n    <h2 class=\"cta-h2\">Try BI1 free.<br><em>Buy the rest if it works.</em>\n</h2>\n    <p class=\"cta-body\">Download Big Idea 1 at no cost. Use it in your classroom. If your students are better prepared for the way the AP exam actually phrases its questions, the full course is $249.</p>\n    <div class=\"cta-row\">\n      <a href=\"/products/ap-csp-teacher-superpack\" class=\"btn-cta\">Get the Full Superpack — $249 →</a>\n      <a href=\"/products/ap-csp-big-idea-1-superpack-free\" class=\"btn-cta-outline\">Free BI1 Preview</a>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"cta-note\">One-time · Instant delivery · Updates through summer 2026</div>\n  </div>\n\n</main>"}